  },
  "kl_at_that_token_against_the_cpu": {
   "gpu_alone": 0.8006,
   "zest_split_off": 6.58
  },
  "mean_kl_over_the_four_pieces_against_the_gpu": {
   "gpu_second_run": 0.0,
   "cpu_alone": 0.007823,
   "zest_as_shipped": 0.01098,
   "zest_split_off": 0.014132,
   "zest_as_shipped_without_that_token": 0.002886,
   "zest_split_off_without_that_token": 0.006041,
   "cpu_alone_without_its_largest_token": 0.007287
  },
  "reading": "Not a fault in zest's build: the position is one where the model amplifies any rounding. llama.cpp's own CPU and GPU results differ most at this same token (0.80, the next largest 0.32 and then under 0.1), and zest's variants land anywhere from 0.01 to 1.00. The NPU's 8-bit blocks round more than the GPU's floats, so zest moves furthest. The result is the same with the build before the changes committed here, with chains off and with the quantized-weight kernel, and the GPU repeats itself exactly. Which side a higher-precision file of the model agrees with was not checked."
 },
